WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.828
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
This week, we're

00:00:01.828 --> 00:00:05.200
talking about supercomputers,
magic buttons, and the smartest

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.690
$100 you ever made.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.420
Welcome to This Week in
Cloud, where we serve

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.970
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.570
This year alone, job listings
requiring Google Cloud skills

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.160
shot up by 65%.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.640
And our Professional Cloud
Architect certification

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.180
was named the top-paying
IT certification.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.460
As if you needed any
more encouragement,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.820
we are rolling out the cloud
certification challenge.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.700
Earn your certificate within
12 weeks of signing up

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.740
for the challenge,
and we will give you

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.370
$100 in Google Store credit.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.010
To make it even easier,
you'll get free access

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.740
to courses on
Qwiklabs and Coursera,

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.680
as well as tips on
taking the exam itself.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.590
Well, what are you waiting for?

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.290
Our ability to generate
data is starting

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:56.480
to outpace our
capacity to process it.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.800
But it won't for long,
thanks to EXAScaler,

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.670
an in-cloud system that
Google recently developed

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.920
in partnership with DDN.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.720
This is big news
if you're running

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.060
a high-performance
computing application

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.260
or planning to build anything
AI-intensive in the future.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.170
Read the post to learn more
about the unique benefits

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:21.070
of using EXAScaler jointly
with the Google Cloud Platform,

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:23.920
and see which industries
stand to gain the most.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.740
Then, try it out.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.710
There's good reason to
love event source systems.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:33.070
But we noticed there weren't
any off-the-shelf solutions

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.970
for getting one up and running.

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.580
So we built one.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.920
This guide walks you
through the why and the

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.430
how of bringing an event
source system into being,

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.800
and how to tackle
some key challenges,

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.000
like keeping messages in order,
creating a schema registry,

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.600
and triggering workloads
based on published events.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.010
Check it out.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.890
If you regularly work
with sensitive data,

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.520
you know how important data
loss prevention tools are.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.150
Adding the ability to access
those tools seamlessly

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.570
from within the GCP
services, like BigQuery, just

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.009
makes sense.

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:12.490
Introducing the Scan
With DLP button--

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:15.130
by using Scan with
DLP, you'll be

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:18.190
able to detect common
sensitive data types,

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:22.180
create triggers for automatic
DLP scan scheduling,

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:25.000
publish reports for
further analysis,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.090
and even obfuscate
sensitive data,

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.940
and all without
leaving your database.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:34.240
If you value data
protection and compliance,

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.120
and you love pressing
buttons for a worthy cause,

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.880
try out Scan with DLP today.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.430
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.550
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.260
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.400
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.140
We'll see you in the cloud.

